WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.880
The government shutdown continues,

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.900
longer than any in history.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.515
I'm told,

00:00:04.515 --> 00:00:05.640
this is a crisis!

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.140
Government shutdown crisis.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.880
Another Trump-generated crisis.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:09.820
This crisis.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.220
Crisis! Crisis!

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.980
It’s causing chaos, confusion, pain.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.900
It’s "just too much",

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.260
say the Washington Post and New York Times.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.520
But wait a second,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.060
looking around America,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.820
I have to ask,

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.560
where's that crisis?

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.920
Most everything seems pretty normal.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.370
How is everything today?

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.100
Life goes on.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.000
Pundits speak

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.140
as if government's the most important part of America.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:40.580
But it isn’t.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.480
We need some government, but

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.896
most of life, the best of life,

00:00:44.896 --> 00:00:47.140
goes on without government,

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.660
much of it in spite of government.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.080
Of course, if you are one of the

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.260
800,000 federal workers

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.040
who aren’t being paid, the shutdown

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.280
is a big deal.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.280
Are you freaking kidding me?

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:58.340
Again?

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.060
Seriously?

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.370
The furloughed workers get a lot of attention.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.220
They’re not getting paid.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:05.840
But they will get paid.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.520
They’re always do after shutdown.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.760
Don’t get me wrong,

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.940
the shutdown is a real problem.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.620
Columnist Paul Krugman giggles about it being

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:17.740
“Trump’s Big Libertarian Experiment.”

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.680
But it’s not libertarian.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.440
Government’s endless rules are still in effect,

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.044
and soon workers will be paid

00:01:25.044 --> 00:01:26.480
for not working.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.080
This is a most un-libertarian experiment.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.360
But there are lessons to be learned.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.140
Under President Obama’s shutdown,

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.000
government officials wouldn’t allow people to

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.160
enter public parks.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.420
The National Park Service

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.840
is blocking access to parks and monuments.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:42.780
This shutdown,

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.200
the administration is allowing people in parks,

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.060
so PBS finds a new “crisis."

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.560
Too much garbage.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.900
National Park Services can’t clean up the mess

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.980
until Congress and the President reach

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.140
a spending deal.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.980
But now volunteers sometimes pick up the trash.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:00.220
Private citizens will step in

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.360
to do some things government workers used to do.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.680
The Washington Post finds another problem.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.180
Farmers aren’t receiving government support checks.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.340
But why do farmers even get support checks?

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.120
The purpose of the subsidy

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.240
was to protect the food supply,

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.580
but most fruit and vegetable farmers

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:20.780
don’t get subsidies,

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.020
and they do fine.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:27.360
There’s no shortage of tangerines, pears, or broccoli.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.940
Grain, cotton, and corn farmers

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.940
could suck it up and do fine, too.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.500
Much of government

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.300
we could just get rid of.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.600
The New York Times says,

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.400
“Shutdown Curtails F.D.A. Food Inspections.”

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.400
Oh no!

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:41.920
We'll be poisoned!

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.723
But if you read the smaller print,

00:02:43.723 --> 00:02:46.080
you'd learn that 80% of food inspection

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.340
is done by the Agriculture Department,

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.200
and they’re still inspecting.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.340
But more important,

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.940
the main reason food is safe

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.280
is not government,

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.380
it's competition.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.409
Fear of getting a bad reputation

00:02:58.409 --> 00:03:00.221
inspires most food producers

00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:02.560
to employ more safety inspectors

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.140
than government requires.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.460
Beef carcasses undergo hot steam rinses

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:13.620
and microbiological testing that go well beyond

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:15.040
what government demands.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.180
Yet politicians want us to think

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.160
it’s all about government.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.000
Where government work is needed,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.780
privatize much of it.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.320
Even security work,

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.760
like what the TSA does,

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.841
is done better

00:03:26.841 --> 00:03:28.760
by the private sector.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.340
Go to San Francisco’s airport,

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:32.220
you’ll notice the lines are shorter,

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.060
and they move more quickly,

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.360
and passengers say

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.420
the screeners are nicer.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:40.020
People here are friendly, and willing to help.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.520
Not only are they nicer,

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.960
the TSA acknowledged

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.420
they were better at finding contraband.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.320
That’s because they’re private contractors.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:49.760
They have to be better

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.780
or they might get fired.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.040
Government never fires itself.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.560
We shouldn’t shut down the government

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:56.780
over a dispute

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.060
and you want to shut it down.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.380
You keep talking about it.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.840
The last time Chuck, you shut it down.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.520
No, no, no.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.360
Finally, it’s absurd that this shutdown

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.120
is supposedly about appropriating $5.7 billion dollars

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.520
for part of a border wall.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.960
That’s less than what Washington spends

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.160
every day.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.420
$54 billion dollar increase in the defense budget.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.340
Well the Senate has passed the Farm Bill,

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.800
a multi-billion dollar legislative package.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.600
Our debt will soon reach $22 trillion dollars,

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.325
government squanders money

00:04:26.325 --> 00:04:27.860
on useless things.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.360
They $300,000 studying whether Japanese quail

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:35.320
are more sexually promiscuous on cocaine.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:36.860
So when government workers protest

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:37.540
and say,

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:39.280
we are all essential.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.160
We all are essential!

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:46.440
I say, give us a break!

